 "structural_change": "HWIN21d c21f (c21d geometry + flow pin registers): the c21d gate (dsdv_mu_hwin_c21d-20261019-182825, CTS) moved the worst setup from SRAM Q -> capture D (gone) to INPUT PORT -> per-event config landing flops g_event_broadcast[*].cfg_{w0,w1,rl,addr,attr}_r (f_mw/f_mc ports fan to 16 event copies along the 561.6 um band after a 166.7 ps input delay; -251 -> -206 ps after repair). Fix: pin registers ON at every pin, anchored at the face (io_flop_at_pins): port -> face flop -> one full cycle across the band -> cfg copies. +1 edge on every input, +1 on every output (priced in INBOX). RTL unchanged. Predecessor: HWIN21d main (2nd failed-gate response; c21b gate 175703 post-CTS setup -162.5 ps at payload capture D = SRAM Q -> ~370 um wire -> central band, FF hold -43 ps / 515 at SRAM wd_in = band wdata -> ~370 um -> macro): macro RE-PACK, RTL unchanged. Macros now 12 columns x 7 rows (3 below / 4 above) around one full-width band, max SRAM pin -> band 145.2 um (<=150), so the SRAM Q -> capture and wdata -> wd_in wires shrink ~2.5x; hold repair gets setup slack at wd_in. Event e's 5 macros are 5 consecutive column slots (<=2 adjacent columns); retire/gap SRAMs in the centre. cycles_added 0. Predecessor: HWIN21cb (one failed gate c21 0ef6cdd20: setup -146 ps at SRAM r_addr_in where ra_next = compare -> advance -> next address; std band 38.9%): every early-capture SRAM (16 event payload + 16 attr + retire) now reads from a REGISTERED address ra_r loaded one edge earlier with inc(next pointer) under the next limit (lm <= decode(lw)), computed from registered pointer/limit state as two candidates (hold / advance) with the advance compare only selecting between them in the D cone; the capture register loads the SRAM word only when a registered per-8-bit load copy (= advance last cycle) is set and otherwise holds, taking same-address writes via current_hit. r_addr_in and the read/write hit compare are now flop-only cones. Public ABI cycle-exact vs anchor 1e057 (EARLY_MITER every cycle): cycles_added 0. Band 54 -> 48.6 um for 40-60% fill. Predecessor: HWIN21c: private capture package dsdv_mu_hwin_capture_1019 (source 9e7921b40, namespace receipts cbbc9e161: 276 legal + 276 expiry + core 136/136 PASS, NS2 four-state terminal 0) with EARLY_HEAD_CAPTURE=1: every event payload/attr and retire SRAM reads the NEXT head address one edge early (dsdv_mu_hwin_capture_1019_mem_early_capture: ra_next + qualified previous-write forwarding), so the macro Q -> compare cone of the failed cb route (TT -371 ps, 93 macro pairs >405 um) gets a full registered stage. Public ABI cycle-exact vs anchor 1e057 (EARLY_MITER every cycle, all 46 shapes): cycles_added 0. Geometry: expanded 388.8x604.8, band 54 um (was 43.2), upper macro rows moved one 43.2 row; max macro-contact to band 368.7 um (<405). Prior cb kit: CODEX HWIN structural SRAM redesign: 16 independent event payload SRAMs (63b due+pos+user) with independent attribute SRAMs; gap and retire timestamp in SRAM. 64x16 true1R1W macros banked84total, registered write ports and previous-write forwarding. Due precomputed at record, final comparator registered due==tm+1. Binary shadow address pointers drive only bank read pins. Kept reset-distinct identity copies <=16entries, per-event reset regions. Remaining parallel identities1457b; fd752bits are fired-state vectors. No extra output edge or change to D>=nw+2. Inactive events enabled only by offset bootword; parameter-free die master16rows. Outline pin/halo constrained475.2x432, macros on43.2grid with10.8halo. Regions successor: same-edge reset-distinct per-event time/wrap/config/address state, per24 RX identity pin copies, registered per12-bit one-hot output selects and endpoint-local collision reductions. All latency edges preserved; strict fanout and actual sizing remain measured gate checks. Central-band geometry successor:8columns x11rows, centralrow skipped for full-width y248.4..291.6 register band. Clock and reset on W beside band; no RTL/reset/data-edge changes. Production parent-fit and measured wire/clock/timing remain owed. HEAD_STAGE=1 captures each fresh head payload unconditionally beside its existing registered winner; output edge and minimum D unchanged. Prune standard rows to the full-width declared band before tapcell. GPL-only row envelope restores full paid physical core and all 84 fixed macro placements before downstream stages. COMPACT_PTR1 uses two reset-distinct same-edge binary pointer copies for two decoder halves. CHECK_STAGE1 evaluates exact next configuration state into local validation flags, preserving first-start fault edge. Default CHECK_STAGE0 remains the direct reference; low/high invalidD fixtures and47slot wrap compare all outputs/faults every cycle.",
